<h4>1. Workforce automation leads to effective on-boarding of employees</h4>
According to researchers, it is found out that on an average basis 20% of employee turnover happens in the span of the initial 45 days. An efficient process of on-boarding the employees is crucial in order to reduce the stated figure.</p><p>

An effective on-boarding process will also allow a venture to identify the duration that an employee would require in order to reach his or her full productivity. It is usually estimated to be in between eight to twelve months. A longer and organised on-boarding process can actually reduce the time which the employee would need in order to reach his or her full potential.</p><p>

Further, a standardized and an efficient process of on-boarding employees ensures over 54% productivity from the newly joined employees, as per research.

Workforce automation can aid companies from various industries to improve their process of on-boarding. This can be achieved by creating automated workflows.</p><p>

If a good workforce automation crm software is employed, it can easily track the details of the employees as well as the responsibilities allocated to them. Therefore, it makes it easy for a newly joined employee to be able to understand and execute his or her primary objective in a better way.</p><p>

<h4>2. Workforce automation Improves productivity</h4>
This is something that we have already discussed briefly; however, here we will look into it rather deeply. Workplace productivity in general remains low. This is not something directly attributed to ventures or industries, rather the diversified needs of the market which are dynamic. Therefore, every venture irrespective of their size or industry needs to find ways to boost up their workplace productivity if they intend to surpass their competitors.</p><p>

If we consider the research obtained around the world, an average employee spends over 520 hours per year to perform tasks that are repetitive in nature and can be easily automated. If we consider tasks like organizing a meeting, scheduling an interview or managing reimbursements, they may appear simple on the surface level but it takes away time from the key objectives which go unnoticed.</p><p>

Workforce automation therefore is a great way of ensuring an enhanced productivity. It organised all the necessary data in a centralized place which is easily accessible. Further, the tasks can be easily automated which ensures a reduction in the amount of labor. Workforce automation enhances productivity and time management.</p><p>

<h4>3. Faster growth</h4>
Each and every venture ultimately aims to be productive, workforce automation enhances productivity and ensures growth. Higher productivity implies an enhanced value of the product or the service that a company is offering. An increased value implies retention of the existing consumers and attracting more of the prospective consumers. All of this directly contributes to the generation of more revenue. This is something every venture thrives for.</p><p>

